  "caption": "Quinn binge-watched a whole season and stood up with a deep ache in the bum. Long drives made it worse; walking oddly helped.\n\nDeep buttock pain is often blamed on the piriformis, but an irritated nerve, the hamstring tendon, the hip or the lower back can all cause similar pain. That's why an assessment matters.\n\nThings that may help: break up long sitting, use a cushion on hard seats, go easy on hard ball rolling, try gentle nerve glides, and build hip and trunk strength.\n\nGet it checked if pain travels below the knee, gets worse with coughing or bending, or comes with numbness or weakness. Saddle numbness or bladder or bowel changes need urgent medical care.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
